An instance is no longer dropped from the inference results when its class was
already inferred for the same name, so a class rebound to an instance of itself
(``MyDict = MyDict()``) infers to both when it is imported from another module.
This fixes false positives such as ``unsupported-membership-test`` on the
imported name.

Refs #3400
Closes pylint-dev/pylint#9846
